U2W: Carlinkit vendor hostapd contract

Makes this hostapd a drop-in for the vendor /usr/sbin/hostapd used by the closed CarPlay daemons:
- parses the unchanged vendor /etc/hostapd.conf (WPS-only device_name/manufacturer accepted and
  ignored in this non-WPS build);
- builds the Apple CarPlay IE (OUI 00:A0:40) like the vendor RTL 0.8.x and BCM v2.7 hostapds and
  adds it to beacons, probe responses and association responses, unless vendor_elements or
  assocresp_elements are configured. The Bluetooth MAC is retried from hci0 for 30 s and the
  beacon refreshed once known. Deviation: the attribute-0 band bit follows the configured band
  (the vendor hard-codes 5 GHz);
- writes /tmp/wifi_status (pair_start / pair_success / disconnected) and /tmp/wifi_connection_list
  with the vendor shell commands at association, authorization and station removal.
Prior art: u2w-build/CARPLAY-HOSTAPD-SOURCES.md.

